{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/100043-methuselah-and-the-technocracy","id":100043,"title":"Methuselah and the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-27T08:34:31-07:00","id":100043,"title":"Methuselah and the Technocracy","content":"This is a question that I've had to chew on periodically, and while I don't think there's a single &quot;correct&quot; answer I'd like to hear people's perspectives.<br /> <br /> A recurring theme of the WoD has generally been that the world secretly serves hidden masters with terrible agendas and vast conspiracies. Peaking behind the curtain, the two groups that fit that role best are the Technocracy and the Vampires. Is there enough room in this town for the both of them? How many puppet-masters can be pulling strings at once before things get tangled up? While their respective grand schemes tend to be in very different areas its not impossible that there's fairly little overlap, but one must assume that they've crossed paths at least a handful of times. How do you think they interact? Who holds a greater claim to being the shadowy lords of all creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T08:51:15-07:00","id":100061,"title":"","content":"Methuselahs are not one unified force. Methuselah and all vampires often overlap their influences into each others respective pies. The Technocracy however are theoretically all in the same Technocratic Union.<br /> <br /> So I would wager they do overlap. The books say the Technocracy Turns a blind eye threats that stable and not as cancerous to humanity. Vampires basically propagate the same mistakes humans do, most don't cultivate demons intentionally. The Methuselahs are individuals, with individual plans. Remember Baba Yaga falls under this discussion as an example of Methuselah behavior, she very clearly would have been a problem for the local Technocrats.<br /> <br /> Vampires in general are concerned about temporal power. Technocrats are concerned about Temporal power as well as other things such as influence over the hearts and minds of all of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T09:54:13-07:00","id":100116,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that at least of Revised forward WoD the various factions of the splats have <i>influence</i> not <i>control</i>, which is a significant difference. The modern world is at once too big and too complex for any single party to take control.<br /> <br /> Consider ghouling say the US President. Huzzah you command the most powerful man on the planet right? Well yeah but you also need to ghoul a lot of Congress to enact the legislation you want, and your Presidential ghoul is going to be a damaged asset in no more then a mere 8 years, plus you have to get them re-elected in the middle of that so better keep everyone happy. And can't exactly dispose of the guy afterward as easily. And how long would a President remain in office if you just bombed each and every enemy by having B-52 strikes ordered?<br /> (Oh and what happens when a public figure doesn't age? And how much of the staff do you also need influence to remain unnoticed)<br /> <br /> That's not even getting into being opposed by other parties. Especially more then one who also have conflicting interests.<br /> <br /> So you're basically force back to more subtle but less powerful methods. Sure you can throw money around or get the occaisonal favor traded... but there's plenty of that to go around. I believe the official figure is something like 1:100,000 vamps:mortals and I can't imagine any other ratio is that different.<br /> <br /> So plenty of room for everyone to play their games, many of them end up cancelled out or superceded by larger events.<br /> <br /> (Nitpick: Methuselah aren't all that likely to care about things as temporary as mortal governments, they'll manipulate their childer into caring for them while they're off pursuing how to diablerize God/Caine/Antidiluvians or survive Gehenna or wipe out the thin-bloods that bring Gehenna closer.... but anyways)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2594-solomon-black","user":"Solomon Black","date":". 03-27-2014, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2594-solomon-black","name":"Solomon Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:02:01-07:00","id":100369,"title":"","content":"The thing to understand about Methuselahs is that they are fairly epic on levels of not giving a shit. Vampires care about blood (which in the case of the Methuselahs means making sure there are enough vampiric snack-cakes running around for when they wake up), not having their resting places discovered, and hunting their enemies in the Jyhad. They do not particularly care about the ups and downs of humanity, wars, taxes, or treaties. Mostly their agendas take place in the ancient and hidden parts of the world.<br /> <br /> Conversely the Technocracy is knee-deep in humanity, and isn't concerned with the ancient and arcane - that's old news. Secret places don't mold minds, and old worn-out places aren't relevant to modern society. The war for them is fought in Silicon Valley, not the Nile Valley. They don't care about some vampiric conflict - let the bloodsuckers destroy each other anyway, because once we turn the Consensus the right way they'll all fade out anyway.<br /> <br /> Two things to keep in mind:<br /> <br /> First, both groups no relatively little about each other. No one has ever sat a vampire and Technocrat down and hashed out all their differences; nobody in either group has read the game book. Neither probably is aware of the true capabilities of the other.<br /> <br /> Second, both groups influence, but do not control. They are simply two large factors among a host of large factors. They can coexist much as other multiple influences can coexist.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}